<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan yarn rates end steady, seen stable.</title>
<headline>Pakistan yarn rates end steady, seen stable.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan cotton yarn rates ended steady on Thursday amid depressed yarn demand and dealers said prices would remain stable next week amid steady conditions in the domestic cotton market.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Thursday     Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    460	    460</p>
<p>    Popular (Shabaz)	   440	    440</p>
<p>    Din Tex.		     465	    465</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.56 rupees)    -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
